# Architecture Rules

Keep these layers separate:

1. Curriculum
2. Recording
3. Transcription
4. Confidence filtering
5. Rubric evaluator
6. AI feedback
7. Progress tracking

The LLM must never be the source of truth for correctness.

Correctness must be determined by evaluator logic using structured transcription results and lesson rubrics.

Use TypeScript types for shared data contracts.

Prefer small, testable modules.

Do not create circular dependencies.

Do not call AI inside evaluator functions.
